248   c  TITL$NUCLEAR DATA SHEETS FOR A=248                                     
248   c  AUTH$C.D. Nesaraja                                                     
248   C  CIT$NDS 204, 374 (2025)                                                
248   c  INST$Physics Division,                                                 
248  #c       Oak Ridge National Laboratory,                                    
248  #c       Oak Ridge, Tennessee 37831-6354, USA                              
248   c  ABST$Available information pertaining to the nuclear structure of      
248  2c  ground and excited states for all known nuclei with mass numbers A=248 
248  3c  has been compiled and evaluated. The adopted level and decay schemes,  
248  4c  as well as the detailed nuclear properties and configuration           
248  5c  assignments based on experimental data, are presented for these        
248  6c  nuclides. When there are insufficient data, expected values from       
248  8c  systematics of nuclear properties and/or theoretical calculations are  
248  9c  utilized. Unexpected or discrepant experimental results are also       
248  ac  noted.  This work supersedes the 2014 evaluation by M.J. Martin        
248  bc  (2014Ma86).                                                            
248   c  COMM$The statistical analysis of |g-ray data and deduced level schemes 
248  2c  is carried out through a suite of computer codes available at          
248  3c  IAEA-Nuclear Data Section web page. The direct feedings to excited     
248  4c  states in |b{+-} and |e decays have generally been computed from       
248  5c  I(|g+ce) intensity balances at each level; the associated log {Ift}    
248  6c  values are calculated using the BetaShape code.  Theoretical total     
248  7c  conversion coefficients are calculated using the BrIcc code (2008Ki07) 
248  8c  for the "Frozen-orbitals" option. The AlphaHF code has been used to    
248  9c  calculate hindrance factors and nuclear radius parameters for alpha    
248  ac  decay                                                                  
248   c  CUT$All literature available up to June 30, 2024 have been considered. 
248  2c  The NSR database (2014Pr09) (www.nndc.bnl.gov/nsr/) is the primary     
248  3c  source for the bibliography.                                           
248   c  ACKN$The use of the XUNDL database has greatly helped to reduce the    
248  2c  evaluation time. The evaluator is appreciative of the reviewer's       
248  3c  insightful comments offered in the review of this manuscript.          
248   c  FUND$Research sponsored by Office of Nuclear Physics, Office of        
248  xc  Science, US Department of Energy under contract DE-AC05-00OR22725.     

