248CM c  2019Sh34: Inelastic reaction with heavy ions was used to study         
248CM2c  the K isomer of {+248}Cm. E({+209}Bi)=1450 MeV from the ATLAS          
248CM3c  superconducting heavy-ion accelerator at Argonne National Laboratory   
248CM4c  impinged a 200 |mg/cm{+2} {+248}Cm target. Gamma rays were measured    
248CM5c  using the 4|p Gammasphere array consisting of 101 Compton-suppressed   
248CM6c  HPGe detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, |g|g(t). Time distribution of 
248CM7c  |g rays depopulating the K{+|p}=8- isomer was done by utilizing the    
248CM8c  different beam-off time intervals. Deduced T{-1/2} of the K{+|p}=8-    
248CM9c  isomer.                                                                
248CM cG E$From Figure 3 in 2019Sh34, except as noted.                          
248CM2cG Authors have not provided any uncertainties                            
248CM cG E(B)$From level energy difference. Gamma transition not indicated in   
248CM2cG Figure 3 of 2019Sh34                                                   
248CM cL E,J$From Figure 3 in 2019Sh34                                          
248CM CL BAND(A)$g.s. band                                                      
