248CM    248CM(A,A'),(D,D')            1975TH11,1975YA13         25NDS    202507
248CM  H TYP=FUL$AUT=C.D. Nesaraja$CIT=NDS 204, 374 (2025)$CUT=30-Jun-2024$     
248CM c  1975Th11: E(d)=15 MeV. FWHM |? 8 keV. |q=90|', 125|'                   
248CM c  1975Ya13: E(d)=16 MeV. FWHM |? 14 keV. |q=90|', 125|'                  
248CM2c  E(|a)=29 MeV. |q=125|'                                                 
248CM c  B(EL) values given here are from 1975Th11. The values were             
248CM2c  normalized to B(E3)(1095 level)=0.41, obtained in Coulomb excitation,  
248CM3c  but note that the uncertainty of 0.10 in this normalization            
248CM4c  value is not included                                                  
248CM cL E$From 1975Ya13, except where noted otherwise                          
248CM cL E(Y)$The peak at 1050 has a B(E2) value agreeing with that for a       
248CM2cL 2+ excitation at this energy in Coulomb excitation, suggesting         
248CM3cL that the main contribution to this peak is from this same 2+           
248CM4cL level; however, based on the members of the K|p=1- band seen in        
248CM5cL Coulomb excitation beginning at the 7- member (E=1295), and with       
248CM6cL the assumption that the 3- and 5- band members are the levels seen     
248CM7cL here at 1095 and 1172, respectively, the 1- bandhead energy is         
248CM8cL expected at 1050. The peak at this energy in (d,d') thus               
248CM9cL possibly includes both a 2+ and a 1- level                             
