248CF    249CF(18O,19OG)               2022OR04,2010TA10         25NDS    202507
248CF  H TYP=FUL$AUT=C.D. Nesaraja$CIT=NDS 204, 374 (2025)$CUT=30-Jun-2024$     
248CF c  Includes: Cf({+18}O,xn|g) and {+249}Cf({+208}Pb,{+209}Pb|g).           
248CF c  XUNDL work for 2022Or04 compiled by B. Singh (McMaster), April 27,     
248CF2c  2023 has been incorporated along with the work of 2010Ta10 by the      
248CF3c  evaluator.                                                             
248CF c  2022Or04 : Single neutron transfer reaction was performed with         
248CF2c  E({+18}O)=140.4 MeV beam from the Japan Atomic Energy Agency-Tokai     
248CF3c  tandem accelerator. The target consisted of 104 |mg/cm{+2} thick       
248CF6c  radioactive {+249}Cf electrodeposited on a |?270 |mg/cm{+2}            
248CF7c  thick nickel foil. Measured E|g, I|g, ({+19}O)|g-coin,                 
248CF2c  |g|g-coin, lifetimes of isomers by |g|g(t) using Si array of ten       
248CF3c  |DE-E telescopes for {+19}O, four Ge detectors and four LaBr{-3}(Ce)   
248CF4c  detectors for |g radiation. Deduced high-spin levels, J|p, isomers,    
248CF8c  B(E1), and Nilsson configurations.                                     
248CF c  2012HoZW: High-spin states were populated via the 1n transfer          
248CF2c  reaction {+249}Cf({+208}Pb,{+209}Pb|g) at Argonne National             
248CF3c  Laboratory. The |g rays emitted were detected with 101                 
248CF4c  Compton-suppressed, HPGe detectors of the Gammasphere spectrometer.    
248CF5c  The level scheme with g.s. band up to 28+ and octupole band up to      
248CF6c  25- was proposed.                                                      
248CF7c  In an email communication with P. Chowdhury on 27 August,              
248CF8c  2024, the evaluator was advised not to use the data in the thesis.     
248CF9c  The data needs to be corrected and will be published by the authors.   
248CFac  Hence, the evaluator has not included the work of 2012HoZW in this     
248CFbc  dataset.                                                               
248CF c  2010Ta10: Neutron transfer reaction was performed with E({+18}O)=153   
248CF2c  MeV beam from the Japan Atomic Energy Agency-Tokai tandem accelerator  
248CF3c  facility. The target consisted of 63% {+249}Cf, 13% {+250}Cf,          
248CF4c  and 24% {+251}Cf. Outgoing nuclei were detected using four sets of     
248CF5c  Si |DE-E detectors. |g rays were measured using six Ge                 
248CF6c  detectors in coincidence with the outgoing nuclei. Measured E|g, I|g.  
248CF7c  Deduced levels, J, |p.                                                 
248CF cG $In the Table below, the intensities of x rays are relative to 100     
248CF2cG for the 550.6-keV |g rays. The K|a and K|b x rays were unresolved      
248CF3cG in the LaBr{-3} spectrum (2022Or04)                                    
